Drop the Ripgrep WORKSPACE stanzas

WORKSPACE.linux loads //Vendors/Ripgrep:repositories.bzl, but
Vendors/Ripgrep is not in SYNCLIST and the public repository does not
contain it. The load fails before any target can be built. Nothing outside
the two WORKSPACE files uses ripgrep, so the load, the ripgrep_repositories()
call and the @ripgrep_crates load are removed.

ripgrep_repositories() also called rules_rust_dependencies(), which declared
rules_license 1.0.0 before the apple and swift rule sets could declare
0.0.3. protobuf 32.0 calls license() without license_kinds, which 0.0.3
requires, so without that declaration every //Apps target fails analysis.
rules_license is now pinned beside protobuf and rules_cc.
